{
  "assembly_notes": "One carcass part carries the case shell, the support base, the runner rails and the centre divider; every drawer is a separate moving hollow tray. The host publishes a plan profile and a clear opening, so each drawer front is struck from the host's own front curve over its own x-range and each level derives its width, graduated height, depth and travel from the cavity and from N. Runners stay engaged with their rails through the full stroke, so no combination is excluded and no overlap allowance is emitted.",
